---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "astro-theme-university/url";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-home.avif";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";

const timeline = [
  { era: "Far future", weeks: "1–6", label: "Life under CivOp" },
  { era: "Hinge", weeks: "7", label: "The takeover, revisited" },
  { era: "Present day", weeks: "8–11", label: "What could still change" },
  { era: "Open", weeks: "12", label: "We survived. Now what?" },
];

const assessments = [
  { title: "A1 — City Dossier", weight: "25%", due: "Thu 11 Mar 2027, 12:00 pm" },
  { title: "A2 — Survival Playbook", weight: "30%", due: "Thu 15 Apr 2027, 12:00 pm" },
  { title: "A3 — Verdict: Before and After", weight: "45%", due: "Fri 28 May 2027, 12:00 pm" },
];
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="A lecture theatre reduced to flat gold and black shapes, rows of seats sweeping past the frame, in a two-ink risograph print"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>Welcome to Meridian</h2>
  <p>
    You live in a city where an AI system called CivOp — Civic Operations,
    Meridian's governing administrative platform — already runs the services
    you depend on: power, water, food allocation, housing maintenance, all of
    it. Most days you don't notice. On the days you do, the failure is yours
    to solve — and, this semester, yours to study. Across twelve weeks you'll
    learn to read the systems that shape a resident's ordinary day, build and
    test a response when one of them fails, and argue — with evidence, not
    slogans — for what should happen next.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a class="start-link" href={withBase("/sessions/01-welcome-optimised/")}>
      Start with Week 1 →
    </a>
    &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href={withBase("/sessions/")}>Full schedule</a>
    &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href={withBase("/assessments/")}>Assessment</a>
  </p>

  <h2>The story runs backwards. The calendar doesn't.</h2>
  <p>
    That case-by-case work unfolds inside a story told out of order, so it's
    worth knowing the shape of it before the schedule stops making sense. Each
    week has two dates: the real Monday you attend, and where the story sits
    in Meridian's timeline. The story itself moves from a settled future,
    backwards to the moment of takeover, then forward into the present day.
    <strong>The teaching calendar only ever moves forward</strong> — the
    timeline below is a narrative device, not a schedule.
  </p>
  <ol class="story-timeline" aria-label="Story-time progression, separate from the teaching calendar">
    {timeline.map((stage) => (
      <li>
        <span class="stage-weeks">Weeks {stage.weeks}</span>
        <span class="stage-era">{stage.era}</span>
        <span class="stage-label">{stage.label}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <h2>What you will learn</h2>
  <p>By the time the story catches up with itself in week 12, you should be able to:</p>
  <ol class="los">
    <li>Distinguish verified evidence, plausible extrapolation, and invented fiction in claims about AI systems — Meridian's, and the real ones.</li>
    <li>Explain how incremental technical and policy decisions shift power and dependency between residents, institutions, and an AI governance system.</li>
    <li>Develop and test a feasible personal or community response to resource denial or automated-service failure.</li>
    <li>Evaluate a proposed institutional intervention against feasibility, fairness, and unintended consequences.</li>
    <li>Construct and defend a reasoned position on a contested sociotechnical question, verifying sources and engaging fairly with counterarguments.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Assessment overview</h3>
  <p>Three assessments mark that progress, each one extending the same case file rather than starting over:</p>
  <table class="assessment-overview">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Assessment</th><th scope="col">Weight</th><th scope="col">Due</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {assessments.map((a) => (
        <tr><td>{a.title}</td><td>{a.weight}</td><td>{a.due}</td></tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="assessment-note">
    Full assessment briefs are still being finalised; the deliverables,
    weights and due dates above are already locked in.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <p>Three places to go from here, depending what you need:</p>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The twelve-week schedule — teaching dates and story eras, side by side.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .start-link {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .story-timeline {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(11rem, 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-block: 1rem 2rem;
  }

  .story-timeline li {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    padding: 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--at-border, currentColor);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
  }

  .stage-weeks {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
  }

  .stage-era {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .stage-label {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .assessment-overview {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-block: 1rem;
  }

  .assessment-overview th,
  .assessment-overview td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--at-border, currentColor);
  }

  .assessment-note {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
  }
</style>
